1
00:00:07,350 --> 00:00:10,914
We know that propose and reject always stops.

2
00:00:10,914 --> 00:00:13,900
But stopping is not the same as succeeding.

3
00:00:13,900 --> 00:00:20,620
When it stops, is every job really paired with a candidate, and every candidate with a job?

4
00:00:20,783 --> 00:00:22,645
Here is what could go wrong.

5
00:00:22,645 --> 00:00:27,170
In the first episode Control was refused by Anita and then by Bridget,

6
00:00:27,170 --> 00:00:30,725
and it ended with the last name on its list, Christine.

7
00:00:30,725 --> 00:00:34,121
What if Christine had refused it too?

8
00:00:34,283 --> 00:00:38,883
Then Control would have no name left, and it could never make an offer again.

9
00:00:38,883 --> 00:00:45,625
So let us suppose that this happens to some job on some day, and look closely at the end of that day.

10
00:00:46,783 --> 00:00:52,113
Each candidate who refused Control did so because she kept an offer she liked more.

11
00:00:52,113 --> 00:00:58,213
And by the improvement lemma she still holds Control or something better at the end of every later day.

12
00:00:58,213 --> 00:01:04,127
It cannot be Control itself, which she has refused, so she holds another job.

13
00:01:04,283 --> 00:01:10,655
So at the end of that day all three candidates hold an offer, and none of the three offers is from Control.

14
00:01:10,655 --> 00:01:17,113
A job makes only one offer each morning, so three hands need three different jobs.

15
00:01:17,283 --> 00:01:22,651
But without Control only two jobs are left, Approximation and Basis.

16
00:01:22,651 --> 00:01:25,495
Two jobs cannot fill three hands.

17
00:01:25,495 --> 00:01:31,731
So the day we supposed can never come, and Control cannot be refused by everyone.

18
00:01:31,883 --> 00:01:35,105
The same count works for any number of jobs.

19
00:01:35,105 --> 00:01:40,081
A job refused by everyone would leave one job fewer than there are candidates,

20
00:01:40,081 --> 00:01:43,143
while every candidate holds an offer of her own.

21
00:01:43,143 --> 00:01:46,811
So no job ever runs out of names.

22
00:01:46,983 --> 00:01:50,631
So every morning every job has someone to ask.

23
00:01:50,631 --> 00:01:56,491
On the last day nobody is refused, so every job's offer is in the hand of some candidate.

24
00:01:56,491 --> 00:02:03,031
No candidate holds two offers, and there are as many candidates as jobs, so everyone is paired.

25
00:02:03,031 --> 00:02:07,189
Propose and reject always ends with a matching.

26
00:02:09,150 --> 00:02:12,820
Now the main question, whether that matching is stable.

27
00:02:12,820 --> 00:02:18,826
Here is the result of the first episode, with the two names that Control crossed off shown faded.

28
00:02:18,826 --> 00:02:22,107
Approximation and Basis have their first choices,

29
00:02:22,107 --> 00:02:26,326
so the only job that would rather have someone else is Control.

30
00:02:26,483 --> 00:02:30,857
Control would rather have Anita, who is above its partner Christine.

31
00:02:30,857 --> 00:02:35,151
Now, why is Anita above Christine and yet not its partner?

32
00:02:35,151 --> 00:02:41,031
A job works down its list, and it only moves past a name when that name has refused it.

33
00:02:41,031 --> 00:02:45,757
So Control asked Anita on an earlier day, and she said no.

34
00:02:45,916 --> 00:02:48,410
Now the improvement lemma speaks.

35
00:02:48,410 --> 00:02:54,798
From the day Control asked her, Anita holds Control or something better at the end of every day,

36
00:02:54,798 --> 00:02:56,860
and that includes the last day.

37
00:02:57,016 --> 00:03:02,980
And on the last day she does not hold Control, because Control's last offer went to Christine.

38
00:03:02,980 --> 00:03:09,234
So what Anita holds at the end is a job she likes more than Control, and she has no wish to leave it.

39
00:03:09,234 --> 00:03:13,066
Control and Anita are not a rogue couple.

40
00:03:13,250 --> 00:03:18,172
Bridget is the other name above Christine, and the same steps apply to her.

41
00:03:18,172 --> 00:03:23,834
Control asked her on day two and she refused, so she ends with Control or better.

42
00:03:23,834 --> 00:03:29,118
It is not Control, so it is Basis, which is higher on her list.

43
00:03:31,083 --> 00:03:33,787
Nothing in those steps used the names.

44
00:03:33,787 --> 00:03:39,225
Take any job with its final partner, and any candidate the job would rather have.

45
00:03:39,225 --> 00:03:46,107
She stands above the partner on its list, so the job asked her on an earlier day and she refused.

46
00:03:46,283 --> 00:03:50,585
By the improvement lemma she ends with that job or a better one.

47
00:03:50,585 --> 00:03:54,763
It is not that job, because its last offer went to its partner.

48
00:03:54,763 --> 00:03:59,461
So she ends with a job she likes more, and she will not leave it.

49
00:03:59,616 --> 00:04:05,998
A rogue couple needs a job and a candidate who both want to switch, and here the candidate never does.

50
00:04:05,998 --> 00:04:12,020
So the result of propose and reject has no rogue couple, which means it is always stable.

51
00:04:12,020 --> 00:04:18,074
And so a stable matching always exists, which the roommates could not promise.

52
00:04:18,250 --> 00:04:22,754
But in episode three one set of lists had two stable matchings.

53
00:04:22,754 --> 00:04:27,470
So which one does propose and reject choose, and who is it good for?

54
00:04:27,470 --> 00:04:30,084
That is where we go next.

